exp2

. Install Git and verify its installation.
git --version


2. Configure Git username and email.
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your-email@gmail.com"


3. Verify Git configuration.
git config --list


4. Create a new project folder and initialize Git.
mkdir gitproject
cd gitproject
git init


5. Check the repository status.
git status


6. Create a README file.
echo "My First Git Project" > README.md


7. Add files to the staging area.
git add .


8. Commit the changes.
git commit -m "Initial Commit"


9. Create a GitHub repository named Git-Practical-2.
10. Connect the local repository to GitHub.
git branch -M main
git remote add origin <GitHub-Repository-URL>


11. Push the code to GitHub.
git push -u origin main


Collaboration Workflow
12. Create a new feature branch.
git switch -c feature/update-readme


13. Modify the README file and add collaboration-related content.
14. Stage and commit the changes.
git add README.md
git commit -m "Updated README using feature branch"


15. Push the feature branch to GitHub.
git push -u origin feature/update-readme


16. Open GitHub and create a Pull Request from feature/update-readme to main.
17. Review and merge the Pull Request.
18. Switch back to the main branch and update the local repository.
git switch main
git pull origin main


19. Verify the repository status.
git status


exp3
Procedure:
1. Install Java JDK on the system.
2. Verify Java installation.
java -version


3. Download Jenkins from the official website: https://www.jenkins.io/download/
4. Select the Windows installer and install Jenkins.
5. Configure Jenkins to run as a Windows service.
6. Start the Jenkins service.
7. Open a web browser and navigate to:
http://localhost:8080


8. Unlock Jenkins using the initial administrator password stored at:
C:\ProgramData\Jenkins\.jenkins\secrets\initialAdminPassword


9. Install the suggested plugins.
10. Create an administrator account.
11. Open the Jenkins Dashboard.
12. Click New Item.
13. Enter the project name as Hello-World.
14. Select Freestyle Project and click OK.
15. Go to the Build Steps section.
16. Select Execute Windows batch command.
17. Enter the following commands:
echo Hello World
echo Welcome to Jenkins
echo Experiment 3 completed successfully


18. Click Save.
19. Click Build Now to execute the job.
20. Open Build History and select the latest build.
21. Click Console Output to view the execution result.
22. Verify that the build finishes successfully.


